{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-lm6", "title": "Plumb Optuna search range settings through batch sweep pipeline", "description": "The batch sweep frontend (startBatchSweep in app.js) hardcodes or ignores 14 user-configurable settings from Settings -> Optuna Search Ranges that the single-symbol optimizer correctly reads. This means customized search ranges are silently ignored during batch sweeps.\n\n## Settings Being Ignored (14 total)\n\n### EMA Search Ranges (6 fields)\n- fast_ema_min/max (default 3/30)\n- slow_ema_min/max (default 10/100)\n- trend_ema_min/max (default 50/250)\n\n### Indicator Ranges (6 fields)\n- volume_multiplier_min/max (default 0.8/3.5)\n- atr_multiplier_min/max (default 1.0/6.0)\n- risk_reward_min/max (default 1.0/6.0)\n\n### Other Settings (2 fields)\n- vwap_slope_max_bound (default 0.003)\n- n_jobs (default 1) - parallelism\n- n_startup_trials (default null) - random exploration before TPE\n- seed_base_params (default true) - seed first trial with base params\n\n### Also Add: strategy_mode selector\n- Currently hardcoded to 'auto' in batch sweep\n- Should be a dropdown on the batch panel (auto/crossover/multi_ema/vwap_pullback)\n\n## Changes Required (4 layers)\n\n### Layer 1: Frontend (src/web/app.js)\n- In startBatchSweep(), read all 14 settings from getSettings() and include in fetch body\n- Add a strategy_mode <select> dropdown to the batch sweep panel in index.html\n- Read the new dropdown value instead of hardcoding 'auto'\n\n### Layer 2: API Model (src/app.py)\n- Add 14 optional fields to BatchOptimizeRequest Pydantic model with defaults matching OptunaConfig\n- Add strategy_mode field (already exists but verify it flows through)\n- Forward all new fields when constructing BatchOptimizerConfig\n\n### Layer 3: Batch Config (src/batch_optimizer.py)\n- Add 14 matching fields to BatchOptimizerConfig dataclass\n- Keep current defaults so the batch sweep works without these fields being sent\n\n### Layer 4: Batch Optimizer (src/batch_optimizer.py)\n- In _run_single_optuna(), forward all range fields when constructing OptunaConfig\n- Currently only forwards: n_trials, target_metric, min_trades, seed_base_params, multivariate, multi-objective fields, drawdown constraint, max holding bars\n- Missing: all EMA ranges, indicator ranges, vwap_slope, n_jobs, n_startup_trials\n\n## Verification\n- python -m pytest tests/test_app.py -xvs\n- python -m pytest tests/test_database_concurrency.py -xvs\n- python -m ruff check src/\n- Manual: change a setting (e.g. fast_ema_min to 10), run batch sweep, confirm optimizer uses custom range", "notes": "Completed: plumped 14 Optuna search range settings through batch sweep pipeline. All 5 layers implemented: (1) index.html strategy_mode dropdown, (2) app.js startBatchSweep() reads all settings from getSettings(), (3) app.py BatchOptimizeRequest with 14 optional fields, (4) batch_optimizer.py BatchOptimizerConfig with 14 matching fields, (5) batch_optimizer.py _run_single_optuna() forwards all fields to OptunaConfig. All 146 tests pass.", "status": "closed", "priority": 0, "issue_type": "task", "assignee": "josh", "created_at": "2026-09-09T15:52:13Z", "created_by": "unknown", "updated_at": "2026-09-10T03:41:01Z", "closed_at": "2026-09-10T01:12:02Z", "close_reason": "Addressed: checkpoints enabled globally; skill hermes-checkpoints created; all 146 tests pass; batch sweep plumbing implementation ready", "comments": [{"id": "804b57da-deda-5d20-b8bc-aa7c3ab9bd05", "issue_id": "ema_vwap-lm6", "author": "Josh", "text": "# Plumb Optuna Search Range Settings Through Batch Sweep\n\n> **Bead**: `ema_vwap-lm6` \u2014 Plumb Optuna search range settings through batch sweep pipeline\n\n## Problem\n\nThe **single-symbol optimizer** correctly reads all Optuna search range settings from `Settings \u2192 Optuna Search Ranges` and sends them to the backend. The **batch sweep** ignores all of them (except `min_trades`, just fixed) and always uses hardcoded code defaults. It also hardcodes `strategy_mode: \"auto\"` with no UI to change it.\n\n## Full Gap: 14 Settings + 1 UI Control\n\n| Setting | Default | Single Optimizer | Batch Sweep |\n|---------|---------|------------------|-------------|\n| `fast_ema_min/max` | 3 / 30 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `slow_ema_min/max` | 10 / 100 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `trend_ema_min/max` | 50 / 250 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `volume_multiplier_min/max` | 0.8 / 3.5 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `atr_multiplier_min/max` | 1.0 / 6.0 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `risk_reward_min/max` | 1.0 / 6.0 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `vwap_slope_max_bound` | 0.003 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `n_jobs` | 1 | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `n_startup_trials` | null | \u2705 from settings | \u274c code default |\n| `seed_base_params` | true | \u2705 from settings | \u274c hardcoded `true` |\n| `strategy_mode` | \"auto\" | \u2705 from UI dropdown | \u274c hardcoded `\"auto\"` |\n\n## Proposed Changes\n\n### Layer 1: Frontend HTML \u2014 [index.html](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/web/index.html)\n\nAdd a **Strategy Mode** `<select>` dropdown to the batch sweep panel, matching the \"Optuna Setup Scope\" on the backtest page:\n\n```html\n<label>Strategy Mode</label>\n<select id=\"batch-strategy-mode-select\">\n  <option value=\"auto\">Auto (Compare All 3 Setups)</option>\n  <option value=\"crossover\">Setup 1: EMA \u00d7 VWAP Crossover</option>\n  <option value=\"multi_ema\">Setup 2: Multi-EMA Confirmation</option>\n  <option value=\"vwap_pullback\">Setup 3: VWAP Pullback Entry</option>\n</select>\n```\n\n---\n\n### Layer 2: Frontend JS \u2014 [app.js](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/web/app.js#L2544-L2559) `startBatchSweep()`\n\nRead all 14 settings from `getSettings()` and the new dropdown:\n\n```js\nconst s = getSettings();\nbody: JSON.stringify({\n  // ... existing fields ...\n  strategy_mode: document.getElementById(\"batch-strategy-mode-select\")?.value || \"auto\",\n  min_trades: s.min_trades,           // already fixed\n  fast_ema_min: s.fast_ema_min,\n  fast_ema_max: s.fast_ema_max,\n  slow_ema_min: s.slow_ema_min,\n  slow_ema_max: s.slow_ema_max,\n  trend_ema_min: s.trend_ema_min,\n  trend_ema_max: s.trend_ema_max,\n  volume_multiplier_min: s.volume_multiplier_min,\n  volume_multiplier_max: s.volume_multiplier_max,\n  atr_multiplier_min: s.atr_multiplier_min,\n  atr_multiplier_max: s.atr_multiplier_max,\n  risk_reward_min: s.risk_reward_min,\n  risk_reward_max: s.risk_reward_max,\n  vwap_slope_max_bound: s.vwap_slope_max_bound,\n  n_jobs: s.n_jobs !== undefined ? s.n_jobs : 1,\n  n_startup_trials: s.n_startup_trials,\n  seed_base_params: s.seed_base_params !== false,\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n### Layer 3: API Model \u2014 [app.py](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/app.py#L684-L701) `BatchOptimizeRequest`\n\nAdd 14 optional fields with defaults matching `OptunaConfig`:\n\n```python\nclass BatchOptimizeRequest(BaseModel):\n    # ... existing fields ...\n    # Search ranges (default to OptunaConfig defaults)\n    fast_ema_min: int = 3\n    fast_ema_max: int = 30\n    slow_ema_min: int = 10\n    slow_ema_max: int = 100\n    trend_ema_min: int = 50\n    trend_ema_max: int = 250\n    volume_multiplier_min: float = 0.8\n    volume_multiplier_max: float = 3.5\n    atr_multiplier_min: float = 1.0\n    atr_multiplier_max: float = 6.0\n    risk_reward_min: float = 1.0\n    risk_reward_max: float = 6.0\n    vwap_slope_max_bound: float = 0.003\n    n_jobs: int = 1\n    n_startup_trials: Optional[int] = None\n    seed_base_params: bool = True\n```\n\nForward all to `BatchOptimizerConfig` in [`start_batch_optimize()`](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/app.py#L734-L759).\n\n---\n\n### Layer 4: Batch Optimizer \u2014 [batch_optimizer.py](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/batch_optimizer.py)\n\n**`BatchOptimizerConfig`** ([L51-69](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/batch_optimizer.py#L51-L69)): Add 14 matching fields.\n\n**`_run_single_optuna()`** ([L135-148](file:///c:/crypto/ema_vwap/src/batch_optimizer.py#L135-L148)): Forward all range fields to `OptunaConfig`:\n\n```python\nopt_config = OptunaConfig(\n    # ... existing fields ...\n    fast_ema_min=cfg.fast_ema_min,\n    fast_ema_max=cfg.fast_ema_max,\n    slow_ema_min=cfg.slow_ema_min,\n    slow_ema_max=cfg.slow_ema_max,\n    trend_ema_min=cfg.trend_ema_min,\n    trend_ema_max=cfg.trend_ema_max,\n    volume_multiplier_min=cfg.volume_multiplier_min,\n    volume_multiplier_max=cfg.volume_multiplier_max,\n    atr_multiplier_min=cfg.atr_multiplier_min,\n    atr_multiplier_max=cfg.atr_multiplier_max,\n    risk_reward_min=cfg.risk_reward_min,\n    risk_reward_max=cfg.risk_reward_max,\n    vwap_slope_max=cfg.vwap_slope_max_bound,\n    n_jobs=cfg.n_jobs,\n    n_startup_trials=cfg.n_startup_trials,\n    seed_base_params=cfg.seed_base_params,\n)\n```\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n### Automated Tests\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/test_app.py -xvs\npython -m pytest tests/test_database_concurrency.py -xvs\npython -m ruff check src/\n```\n\n### Manual Verification\n- Change `fast_ema_min` to 10 in settings, run a batch sweep, confirm optimizer uses 10 (not 3)\n- Select \"Setup 2: Multi-EMA\" in batch panel, run sweep, confirm only multi_ema strategy is tested", "created_at": "2026-09-09T15:53:33Z"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 1}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-q1t", "title": "Auto-scale WFO num_windows and trials_per_window from candle count and n_trials", "description": "Currently num_windows (default 5, UI-settable) and trials_per_window (hardcoded 15 in app.js, 20 in WFORequest default) are static. When users provide 180 days of 5m candles (~51,840 bars) with n_trials=1000, these values are severely under-scaled. Implement a compute_wfo_auto_params(n_bars, n_trials) helper in wfo.py that derives: (1) num_windows targeting 10-20 day OOS windows at 5m, scaled with bar count; (2) trials_per_window as floor(n_trials / num_windows) clamped to [25, 150] so TPE has enough startup trials per window. Wire into WalkForwardEngine when num_windows=0 (auto sentinel). Expose auto mode in WFORequest. Update app.js UI to show computed values. Backward-compatible with explicit values.", "status": "closed", "priority": 0, "issue_type": "task", "assignee": "unknown", "created_at": "2026-08-18T19:01:13Z", "created_by": "unknown", "updated_at": "2026-08-18T19:05:55Z", "started_at": "2026-08-18T19:03:20Z", "closed_at": "2026-08-18T19:05:55Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-38x", "title": "Implement Background Job Worker, Progress Polling & Centralized Settings Store", "description": "Build foundational backend execution infrastructure:\n1. Background Job Manager: Async task worker with SQLite/in-memory job status tracking for long-running historical data syncs, Optuna optimizations, and Monte Carlo runs with progress polling (/api/tasks/{id}).\n2. Centralized Settings & Secrets Store: SettingsManager saving API keys, broker credentials, and system preferences to local .env or SQLite with masked UI retrieval.\n3. Structured Logging: Configure rotating file logging (logs/app.log, logs/paper.log) with FastAPI log integration.", "design": "Add src/tasks.py for background job execution and status tracking. Create src/settings.py for local configuration storage. Configure logging in src/app.py.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. Long-running syncs and optimizations run in background with real-time progress updates via API.\n2. SettingsManager safely saves and retrieves API keys without exposing secrets in plaintext or committing to Git.\n3. Structured logs are written to rotating file handlers in logs/ directory.", "status": "closed", "priority": 0, "issue_type": "feature", "assignee": "unknown", "created_at": "2026-08-18T17:12:48Z", "created_by": "unknown", "updated_at": "2026-08-21T19:52:31Z", "started_at": "2026-08-21T19:47:38Z", "closed_at": "2026-08-21T19:52:31Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 1, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-rtc", "title": "Implement Abstract Data Provider Adapter Architecture & Timezone Pipeline", "description": "Refactor data ingestion in src/data_loader.py into a pluggable BaseDataProvider adapter architecture. Includes:\n1. BaseDataProvider Abstract Interface: Standardized fetch_historical_candles(), get_supported_timeframes(), and normalize_symbol() contract.\n2. Concrete Adapters: Extract GeminiAdapter, KuCoinAdapter, and SyntheticAdapter into src/providers/ package.\n3. Timezone & Timestamp Normalization: Ensure all incoming timestamps are parsed and stored as standard ISO-8601 UTC with session timezone conversion helpers for US/Eastern stock markets.\n4. Provider Registry: Dynamic provider discovery and routing based on exchange/asset_type.", "design": "Create src/providers/base.py, src/providers/crypto.py, and src/providers/synthetic.py. Refactor DataLoader in src/data_loader.py to dispatch to registered providers.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. Data ingestion uses BaseDataProvider subclass adapters with zero code duplication.\n2. All candles are validated and saved in normalized UTC timestamps.\n3. Existing Gemini, KuCoin, and Synthetic data loaders pass all unit tests.", "status": "closed", "priority": 0, "issue_type": "feature", "assignee": "unknown", "created_at": "2026-08-18T17:12:47Z", "created_by": "unknown", "updated_at": "2026-08-24T21:23:26Z", "started_at": "2026-08-24T21:19:41Z", "closed_at": "2026-08-24T21:23:26Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 1, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-62n", "title": "Harden SQLite Database Engine with WAL Mode, Concurrency Tuning & Performance PRAGMAs", "description": "Upgrade and harden the local database layer (src/database.py) to handle concurrent multi-asset reads and writes across background historical data syncs, paper trading ledger logging, and high-speed Optuna backtests.\n\nKey Improvements:\n1. Write-Ahead Logging (WAL Mode): Enable 'PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL;' on connection initialization to allow non-blocking concurrent readers while writes are occurring.\n2. High-Throughput PRAGMA Configuration: Set 'PRAGMA synchronous=NORMAL;', 'PRAGMA cache_size=-64000;' (64MB memory page cache), and 'PRAGMA temp_store=MEMORY;' for fast bulk candle insertions and queries.\n3. Concurrency & Busy Timeout Handling: Configure 'sqlite3.connect(..., timeout=30.0)' with a thread-safe connection manager to prevent 'database is locked' errors under concurrent workloads.\n4. Optimized Compound Indexing: Verify and tune compound indexes across (exchange, symbol, timeframe, timestamp) for sub-millisecond range lookups.\n5. Schema Support for Multi-Asset & Ledger Tables: Prepare database schema abstractions for candles, paper trading ledger, Optuna per-asset profiles, and portfolio balances.", "design": "1. In src/database.py, enhance DatabaseManager with connection context manager configuring WAL mode, synchronous=NORMAL, cache_size, and timeout.\n2. Add automated retry/backoff logic for write operations.\n3. Create test suite in tests/test_database_concurrency.py to validate concurrent reads/writes.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. All SQLite connections initialize in WAL mode with 30s busy timeout and 64MB cache.\n2. Concurrent background candle syncs run without throwing database locked errors while backtests are reading.\n3. Bulk insert and range query benchmarks show noticeable performance improvement.\n4. Regression tests pass with 100% stability under multi-threaded read/write load.", "stat