{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.7", "title": "Repair paper reconciliation checkpoints and atomic settlements", "description": "Recovery compares candle timestamps against pos.updated_time, but database save_paper_position overwrites updated_time with wall-clock time instead of the last processed candle time. This commonly empties the missed-candle range and falls back to only the last ten candles, potentially missing older downtime exits or replaying already-processed bars. Close flows also commit cash transaction, trade history, and position deletion separately, so crashes can leave inconsistent or repeatable settlement state.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Persist a distinct last-processed market-bar timestamp/ID, not a database update wall clock\\n- [ ] Reconcile strictly candles newer than the checkpoint in chronological order, with documented gap-fill and ambiguous-bar rules\\n- [ ] Make recovery idempotent when run repeatedly or after a crash at each settlement step\\n- [ ] Commit cash ledger entry, completed trade, and position closure atomically or via a recoverable transaction/event state machine\\n- [ ] Test stale checkpoints, gaps longer than ten bars, repeated reconciliation, and injected failures between settlement writes", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:22Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:06Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:06Z", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.7", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:22Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}, {"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.7", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.3", "type": "supersedes", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:06Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.8", "title": "Define causal paper fills and stop-gap execution math", "description": "Paper evaluation derives signal from the latest candle and enters at that same candle close; live partial-candle semantics are undocumented. Stop exits use low/high and fill at stop with slippage but do not account for an opening gap through the stop. Entry stop/target sizing uses the unslipped close while the actual entry is slipped. Timeout/manual/take-profit exits apply inconsistent slippage assumptions. Specify the paper execution contract and align live evaluation with recovery behavior.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Specify whether signals use closed candles or live partial candles and when a fill becomes executable\\n- [ ] Calculate stop/target distances from the actual modeled fill price\\n- [ ] Model adverse opening gaps through stop orders using the open when worse than the stop\\n- [ ] Define slippage/fees by order side and exit reason, including market timeout/manual exits versus passive targets\\n- [ ] Add deterministic tests for gaps, signal timing, slipped entry risk, and parity between normal evaluation and reconciliation", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:22Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:06Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:06Z", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.8", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:22Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}, {"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.8", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.4", "type": "supersedes", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:06Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.6", "title": "Make paper candle execution idempotent and profile-safe", "description": "The polling runner may evaluate the same latest candle repeatedly. If a stop closes a position but the latest signal remains active, a later poll can re-enter on that same bar and repeat fees/exits. step_all_active_profiles iterates profiles independently, while positions are keyed only by exchange/symbol; multiple active profiles for one asset can therefore manage the same position using different timeframe/strategy parameters. Define processed-bar and position/profile identity semantics.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Store/derive a durable last-processed candle identity and prevent duplicate entry/exit side effects for repeated polls of one candle\\n- [ ] Define whether only closed candles or live partial candles can trigger signals/fills\\n- [ ] Enforce one active strategy per asset or scope positions and execution state to profile/timeframe identity\\n- [ ] Ensure a position closed by a bar event cannot re-open from that same event unless explicitly intended\\n- [ ] Add repeated-poll, stop-then-same-signal, and multiple-profile same-symbol tests", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:21Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:05Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:05Z", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.6", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:21Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}, {"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.6", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.2", "type": "supersedes", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:05Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.5", "title": "Unify paper equity and long-short PnL math", "description": "Paper equity and return calculations differ by path. PaperLedger.get_total_equity adds cash plus quantity*current_price for every position, which marks shorts with the wrong sign under the engine's reserved-notional model; get_status instead uses cost_basis+unrealized_pnl. evaluate_symbol computes short unrealized percent as entry/current minus one, while other paths use PnL/cost_basis. Automatic exits include entry+exit fees in trade PnL, but close_position_market reports only exit fees. Define one canonical accounting model and share it across sizing, snapshots, automatic/manual/reconciled close, and trade history.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Define and document long/short equity formulas consistent with reserved cash/collateral semantics\\n- [ ] Make PaperLedger.get_total_equity, get_status, and get_balance_snapshot agree for long and short positions\\n- [ ] Use one return-percent denominator/formula for unrealized and realized long/short PnL\\n- [ ] Ensure manual, stop/target, timeout, and reconciliation trade PnL/fees all include the same lifecycle costs\\n- [ ] Add hand-calculated tests for short price rises/falls, long positions, entry/exit fees, and cross-path snapshot equality", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:20Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:04Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:04Z", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.5", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:20Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}, {"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.5", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.1", "type": "supersedes", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:02:04Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0,