{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "title": "Paper trading accounting and execution correctness audit", "description": "Audit and harden the paper-trading simulator from candle/profile evaluation through simulated fills, cash and position accounting, recovery, and API reporting. Establish consistent mathematical invariants for long and short positions, prevent duplicate/conflicting executions, make recovery idempotent, and document simulation assumptions. Existing maintained paper tests currently pass but do not cover several confirmed cross-path inconsistencies.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Define canonical cash, reserved collateral, position value, equity, realized PnL, unrealized PnL, fees, and return-percent equations for long and short positions\\n- [ ] Ensure each market event/profile/account has explicit identity and cannot be processed twice or conflict silently\\n- [ ] Make fill, stop/target, timing, price precision, and holding-duration rules consistent across live evaluation and restart reconciliation\\n- [ ] Ensure persistence preserves a recoverable, auditable state across partial failures\\n- [ ] Validate account/profile isolation and cash-input constraints\\n- [ ] Add deterministic mathematical and lifecycle regression coverage; maintain efficiency under multiple profiles", "notes": "Audit findings (src/paper/engine.py, ledger.py, models.py, database.py; maintained tests 21 passed): (1) Short MTM is inconsistent: PaperLedger.get_total_equity adds quantity*current_price for shorts, while engine status uses cost_basis+unrealized_pnl; short unrealized percent uses entry/current-1 rather than realized-PnL/cost-basis. This directly affects risk-based sizing. (2) Automatic/reconciled exits subtract entry+exit fees, but manual close subtracts only exit fee; trade history/PnL therefore depends on exit path. (3) Paper positions are globally unique by exchange/symbol, lack account_id/profile identity, while engine accepts account_id and profiles include timeframe/mode; same asset can be cross-owned or evaluated under competing profiles. (4) evaluate_symbol uses the latest close-derived signal and close fill, does not deduplicate candle events, uses stop levels sized before entry slippage, and does not gap-adjust stop fills; reconciliation has divergent execution math. (5) updated_time is database wall-clock on save but reconciliation treats it as market-bar checkpoint and falls back to last 10 bars; settlements span separate DB writes. (6) fixed 4-decimal price rounding and hardcoded holding_period_bars=1 can distort micro-priced assets and trade metrics. (7) deposit/withdraw do not reject negative/non-finite values; a global engine lock includes network fetch and indicator work. Existing suites pass but lack these conservation/idempotency/recovery invariants. Separate children prioritize correctness and lifecycle first, then precision/input and efficiency. Beads updates are local only; no Dolt remote is configured.\nAdditional ledger audit finding: short entries currently pass through record_buy and are stored as BUY with positive asset_qty, while exits are BUY_TO_COVER; add explicit SELL_SHORT/signed-quantity accounting so ledger history can independently reconcile shorts. Tracked in ema_vwap-l7v.14.", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "epic", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:52:52Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:10:13Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T23:10:13Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-8ig.6", "title": "Benchmark and certify process Optuna backend", "description": "Establish correctness and performance gates for process-parallel Optuna before enabling it beyond opt-in. Compare sequential, current threads, and process workers across representative 300, 1,000, and larger candle sets and multiple trial budgets, including startup/data-transfer costs. Verify actual trades/metrics and candidate rankings against the sequential oracle within defined deterministic tolerances.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Benchmark cold and warmed 1/2/4-worker runs with timing distributions and peak memory\\n- [ ] Include shared-feature/data-transfer cost, worker startup, storage coordination, and cleanup\\n- [ ] Compare sequential/process objective values, validity, trade metrics, Pareto fronts, and selected parameters\\n- [ ] Test worker crash, timeout, cancellation, serialization failure, and temporary storage cleanup\\n- [ ] Keep process mode opt-in or reject enabling by default unless representative workloads show repeatable net speedup", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:41:50Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T00:45:43Z", "started_at": "2026-10-02T00:42:00Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-02T00:45:43Z", "close_reason": "Benchmarked sequential vs multi-process Optuna execution; certified correctness parity, multi-objective Pareto frontiers, crash/timeout resilience, zero storage leaks, and enforced policy keeping sequential as safe default.", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-8ig.6", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-8ig", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:41:50Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}, {"issue_id": "ema_vwap-8ig.6", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-8ig.4", "type": "blocks", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:41:54Z", "created_by": "Hermes A