{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-8ig.1", "title": "Decide Optuna process topology and data contract", "description": "Research and specify the supported process-parallel architecture before implementation. Compare Optuna JournalStorage for same-host processes with RDBStorage for multi-node use; do not use SQLite storage for parallel trials. Choose how candles and shared indicator frames are transferred or loaded per worker, how total trial/time budgets and per-worker sampler seeds are allocated, and which execution mode remains the default based on measured throughput.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Document single-host process scope and explicitly defer or specify multi-node support\\n- [ ] Select storage and lifecycle: unique per-study journal or RDB, worker attach/load behavior, cleanup, stale/failed trial policy\\n- [ ] Select a Windows spawn-safe worker entry point and data transport with memory/serialization estimates\\n- [ ] Specify exact total-trial, timeout, cancellation, and per-worker seed semantics\\n- [ ] Record baseline and decision thresholds for keeping sequential as default versus enabling processes", "notes": "Research basis (official Optuna docs): https://optuna.readthedocs.io/en/stable/tutorial/10_key_features/004_distributed.html documents n_jobs as in-process threads and shows multi-process workers coordinating through shared JournalStorage or RDBStorage. It states InMemoryStorage is not process-shared; JournalFileBackend locks are appropriate for same-host local filesystems but not NFS/multi-host; RDBStorage is recommended for multi-node. https://optuna.readthedocs.io/en/stable/reference/generated/optuna.storages.RDBStorage.html explicitly says SQLite is not recommended for parallel optimization. Repository constraints: optimize() currently creates default in-memory studies and defines a nested objective capturing optimizer/config/data/shared-indicator state; API optimization already runs inside TaskManager threads; batch currently loops combinations sequentially. Resolve local single-host Windows spawn topology first; keep multi-node/RDB deployment optional/out of initial scope unless separately justified.", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "spike", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:41:45Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:36:18Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T23:35:28Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T23:36:18Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-8ig.1", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-8ig", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:41:45Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 3, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.3", "title": "Validate multi-objective metrics and exclude invalid trials", "description": "Multi-objective metric names and duplicates are not validated. Invalid or under-traded trials are completed with infinite sentinel values, remain eligible for Pareto selection, and can be emitted as Infinity in top_trials/pareto_frontier. The multi-objective result path marks best_value_valid true unconditionally, even when the selected result is invalid. Validate the objective contract, keep invalid trials out of selection/output, and return an explicit no-valid-result state that remains strict-JSON serializable.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Validate all objective names and reject duplicates before study creation\\n- [ ] Exclude invalid/non-finite and below-min-trade trials from Pareto selection\\n- [ ] Return best_value_valid=false when no valid trial exists\\n- [ ] Ensure top_trials and pareto_frontier contain only finite JSON-safe values\\n- [ ] Add strict JSON serialization tests for all-invalid and mixed-validity studies", "notes": "Multi-objective objective names are canonicalized and validated (including duplicate rejection); no-trade, under-trade, and non-finite trials are pruned rather than assigned infinite objectives; Pareto selection and output include only valid finite trials. All-invalid studies return best_value_valid=false, null values/backtest result, empty top/Pareto lists, and strict-JSON-safe fields. BatchOptimizer now skips this explicit no-valid state. Tests cover invalid config, all-invalid, mixed-validity, non-finite metrics, strict JSON, and batch consumption. Validation: optimizer/API/batch/WFO/parameter-flow set 60 passed; app+WFO order check 17 passed; diagnostics and diff check clean. One full-suite run had a single nondeterministic WFO failure due to a lingering app background optimization consuming a patched test iterator; the WFO test passes alone and with app tests.", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:05Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:34:15Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T02:27:18Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T02:34:15Z", "close_reason": "Validated objective configuration, invalid-trial pruning, finite Pareto output, and safe batch handling with regression tests.", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-pbo.3", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-pbo", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:05Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.2", "title": "Honor sampled stop type and preserve base strategy settings", "description": "The objective samples stop_loss_type but selects the conditional VWAP-offset versus ATR-multiplier branch using the base strategy stop type. Consequently one sampled stop family has its key parameter fixed and the other samples an unused parameter. Candidate StrategyParams are also rebuilt from a partial field list, dropping base settings such as asset_type, session_mode, VWAP anchor, fractional shares, and margin controls. The enqueued baseline omits sampled fields including stop type and trailing distance.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Branch conditional sampling from the trial stop_loss_type, not the base setting\\n- [ ] Build each candidate from the base params and override only optimized fields\\n- [ ] Preserve stock execution, fees, sessions, sizing, and other non-optimized settings\\n- [ ] Ensure seed_base_params enqueues a faithful in-range baseline\\n- [ ] Add tests for both stop types and stock/base-parameter preservation", "notes": "Trial candidates now clone StrategyParams from the base and override only optimized fields, preserving stock/session/VWAP/margin/fees and fixed holding settings. Stop-specific parameters now branch on sampled stop_loss_type. Seeded baselines include stop type and a clamped trailing distance, with existing stop parameters clamped to bounds. Deterministic coverage exercises both stop families, stock/base setting preservation, holding bars, and baseline values. Validation: pytest tests/test_optimizer.py tests/test_wfo.py tests/test_parameter_flow.py -q (37 passed); diagnostics and diff check clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:04Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:27:17Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T02:25:32Z", "closed_at":