{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.1", "title": "Fix single-objective metric direction and ranking", "description": "Single-objective studies are always created with direction=maximize, including ulcer_index where lower is better. Trial summaries are sorted descending regardless of objective direction. This makes the exposed Ulcer Index target optimize the wrong way and reports misleading top trials. Use one metric-direction registry for study creation, selection, and result ordering.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Minimize ulcer_index and maximize all higher-is-better single metrics\\n- [ ] Sort top_trials according to the configured metric direction\\n- [ ] Ensure best_value and best_metric_value correspond to the selected trial and metric\\n- [ ] Add tests where minimizing and maximizing metrics have deliberately opposing trial values", "notes": "Implemented a shared metric-direction policy for study creation and trial ranking: ulcer_index is minimized; higher-is-better single metrics are maximized; multi-objective trial summaries follow the primary objective direction. Deterministic mocked-result tests cover both minimizing ulcer_index and maximizing total_return_pct, including agreement between best_value and best_metric_value. Validation: pytest tests/test_optimizer.py tests/test_new_metrics.py tests/test_wfo.py tests/test_parameter_flow.py -q (39 passed); diagnostics and diff check clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:03Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:25:31Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:16Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T02:25:31Z", "close_reason": "Corrected single-objective Optuna direction and matching trial ranking with deterministic tests.", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-pbo.1", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-pbo", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-0