{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-nom", "title": "Audit paper trading framework and ledger for trade info updates and risk % handling", "description": "Paper trading framework does not update trade information properly or respect the risk % determined by batch sweeping candidates. Audit findings:\n\n# Audit Findings:\n\n## Paper Trading Ledger (`src/paper/ledger.py`)\n\n- **Line 422**: `save_position` method never writes `updated_time` field \u2192 positions show stale/null timestamps\n- **Line 353**: `record_close_position` updates cash balance but doesn't call `close_position()` \u2192 integrity gap between cash and position state\n- **Line 471**: `record_completed_trade` writes trade history but no ledger transaction ID link \u2192 trades lack atomicity from position close\n- **Lines 175, 231, 302**: Buy/sell/short cash record updates but don't update PaperPosition state \u2192 inconsistent state between ledger and position\n\n## Paper Trading Profiles (`src/paper/profiles.py`)\n\n- **Line 117-135**: `_row_to_profile` missing `deployed`/`deployed_at` fields despite being in DB \u2192 deployed flags not persisted\n- **Line 21-52**: `save_profile` accepts `deployed` flag but no batch\u2192profile import \u2192 batch sweep results never populate profiles\n- **Line 91-114**: `get_strategy_params` fallback ignores validated batch results \u2192 risk params not respected in paper trading\n- **Lines 83-85**: `set_active` not tied to validation report status \u2192 manual activation instead of auto from batch validation\n- **Line 72-77**: `list_profiles` only filters `active_only` \u2192 deployed profiles aren't distinguishable from regular active ones\n\n## Paper Trading Engine (`src/paper/engine.py`)\n\n- **Audit pending**: Subagent SA-0 failed with repetition loop \u2192 engine audit incomplete\n\n# Proposed Fixes (to be implemented):\n\n## Ledger Fixes:\n1. Add `updated_time = datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()` write in `save_position`\n2. Call `close_position()` after cash update in `record_close_position`\n3. Add ledger transaction ID link and position removal in `record_completed_trade`\n4. Ensure buy/sell/short record updates also update PaperPosition state\n\n## Profile Fixes:\n1. Add `deployed`/`deployed_at` fields to PaperProfile model\n2. Update `_row_to_profile` to extract these fields from DB rows\n3. Implement `import_batch_result_as_profile()` method for batch sweep integration\n4. Modify `get_strategy_params` to respect validated batch results\n5. Link `set_active` to validation report status\n6. Extend `list_profiles` filtering to include deployment status\n\n# Status:\n- Findings documented: YES (this bead)\n- Code changes: NO (reverted as requested)\n- Subagent audit: SA-1 ledger \u2713, SA-2 profiles \u2713, SA-0 engine \u2717 (needs retry)", "status": "open", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-06T02:54:33Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-06T02:58:00Z", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-609", "title": "Batch Sweep: Add All Combinations option for multi-objective optimization (single-timeframe gate)", "description": "# Batch Sweep: All Multi-Objective Metric Combinations (single-timeframe gate)\n\n## Description\n\nAdd an `\u2605 All Combinations` option to the **Multi-Metric Objective Set** dropdown\n(`#batch-multi-metric-select`) in the Batch Sweep UI. When selected and exactly **one\ntimeframe** is checked, the sweep expands into one sequential sub-run per valid 2-metric\nPareto combination from the allowed multi-objective pool. The gate contract (single\ntimeframe) is identical to the single-objective All Metrics bead.\n\nThis is the multi-objective counterpart to the single-objective \"All Metrics\" bead.\nImplement after (or in parallel with) the single-objective bead.\n\n## Canonical Multi-Objective Metric Pool\n\nSourced from `src/optimizer.py` validation logic:\n`allowed_metrics = TARGET_METRICS | {\"max_drawdown_pct\"}`\n\nFull pool (11 metrics):\n- `sharpe_ratio`, `drawdown_penalized_sharpe`, `calmar_ratio`, `sortino_ratio`,\n  `drawdown_penalized_sortino`, `ulcer_index`, `profit_factor`, `net_profit`,\n  `total_return_pct`, `win_rate`, `max_drawdown_pct`\n\n**Practical curated set for \"All Combinations\"** \u2014 rather than C(11,2) = 55 pairs (which\nwould be prohibitively slow), use a curated list of **high-value pairs** that are\nmeaningfully non-redundant. Recommended default set (12 pairs):\n\n| Pair | Rationale |\n|---|---|\n| `sharpe_ratio\\|max_drawdown_pct` | Risk-adjusted return vs. tail risk |\n| `sharpe_ratio\\|total_return_pct` | Risk-adjusted vs. raw return |\n| `sharpe_ratio\\|win_rate` | Consistency vs. efficiency |\n| `sortino_ratio\\|max_drawdown_pct` | Downside-risk adjusted vs. tail |\n| `calmar_ratio\\|max_drawdown_pct` | Return/DD ratio vs. DD magnitude |\n| `drawdown_penalized_sharpe\\|max_drawdown_pct` | DD-robust Sharpe vs. DD |\n| `drawdown_penalized_sortino\\|max_drawdown_pct` | DD-robust Sortino vs. DD |\n| `profit_factor\\|total_return_pct` | Edge quality vs. total return |\n| `profit_factor\\|max_drawdown_pct` | Edge quality vs. risk |\n| `net_profit\\|max_drawdown_pct` | Absolute profit vs. risk |\n| `total_return_pct\\|win_rate` | Return vs. consistency |\n| `ulcer_index\\|total_return_pct` | Recovery stress vs. return |\n\n> **Design decision required**: Should the set be fixed (hardcoded) or user-configurable\n> (e.g., a checklist of pairs)? This bead assumes the fixed curated 12-pair default.\n> A follow-up bead can add a custom pair builder.\n\n## Backend Changes\n\n### `src/app.py` \u2014 `start_batch_optimize`\n```python\nALL_MULTI_PAIRS = [\n    [\"sharpe_ratio\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"sharpe_ratio\", \"total_return_pct\"],\n    [\"sharpe_ratio\", \"win_rate\"],\n    [\"sortino_ratio\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"calmar_ratio\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"drawdown_penalized_sharpe\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"drawdown_penalized_sortino\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"profit_factor\", \"total_return_pct\"],\n    [\"profit_factor\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"net_profit\", \"max_drawdown_pct\"],\n    [\"total_return_pct\", \"win_rate\"],\n    [\"ulcer_index\", \"total_return_pct\"],\n]\n\nMULTI_ALL_SENTINEL = \"all_combinations\"\n\nif req.enable_multi_objective and req.multi_objective_metrics == [MULTI_ALL_SENTINEL]:\n    if len(req.timeframes) != 1:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=400,\n            detail=\"'All Combinations' multi-objective requires exactly one timeframe.\"\n        )\n    configs = [\n        BatchOptimizerConfig(\n            ...shared fields from req...,\n            enable_multi_objective=True,\n            multi_objective_metrics=pair,\n            target_metric=pair[0],        # reference metric for leaderboard storage key\n        )\n        for pair in ALL_MULTI_PAIRS\n    ]\n    background_tasks.add_task(_run_all_metrics_batch_task, configs)\n    return {\"status\": \"started\", \"message\": f\"All multi-objective combinations started ({len(configs)} pairs).\"}\n```\n\nThe `_run_all_metrics_batch_task` function (defined in the single-objective bead) is reused\nwithout modification \u2014 it is metric-agnostic and works for both single and multi-objective\nconfigs.\n\n### Progress label in current_combo\nFor multi-objective runs, format as:\n`[sharpe_ratio|max_drawdown_pct \u2014 1/12]`\n\n## Frontend Changes\n\n### `src/web/index.html` \u2014 `#batch-multi-metric-select`\nAdd as **first** `<option>`:\n```html\n<option value=\"all_combinations\">\u2605 All Combinations (Single Timeframe Only)</option>\n```\nAdd hint element below the select:\n```html\n<small id=\"batch-all-multi-hint\" style=\"display:none; color: var(--accent-amber);\">\n  \u2605 Runs 12 curated Pareto-pairs. Select exactly one timeframe.\n</small>\n```\n\n### `src/web/app.js` \u2014 `syncBatchMetricUI()` (extend from single-objective bead)\nAdd multi-objective sentinel check:\n```js\nconst multiVal = document.getElementById(\"batch-multi-metric-select\")?.value;\nif (isMultiMode && multiVal === \"all_combinations\") {\n  // same TF-count gate logic as single-objective all_metrics\n}\n```\n\n### `startBatchSweep()` \u2014 payload serialization\nWhen `objectiveMode === \"multi\"` and `multiMetricValue === \"all_combinations\"`:\n```js\nbody: JSON.stringify({\n  ...\n  enable_multi_objective: true,\n  multi_objective_metrics: [\"all_combinations\"],  // sentinel\n  target_metric: \"all_combinations\",              // backend checks this\n})\n```\n\nThe backend intercepts `multi_objective_metrics == [\"all_combinations\"]` before validation\nso the normal `OptunaOptimizer` metric validation is never reached.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `#batch-multi-metric-select` has `\u2605 All Combinations` as first option\n- [ ] Hint element appears when `all_combinations` is selected\n- [ ] Run button disabled (red hint) when `all_combinations` + multiple timeframes\n- [ ] Run button enabled (amber hint) when `all_combinations` + exactly one timeframe\n- [ ] Backend receives sentinel `multi_objective_metrics: [\"all_combinations\"]` and expands to 12 pairs\n- [ ] Backend returns HTTP 400 if sentinel + `len(timeframes) != 1`\n- [ ] Each pair sub-run saves its own leaderboard row with `target_metric` = `\"pair[0]|pair[1]\"` format\n- [ ] Progress label shows `[metric1|metric2 \u2014 N/12]`\n- [ ] `_run_all_metrics_batch_task` is reused without forking (no duplication)\n- [ ] All 451 existing tests pass; add \u22651 unit test for the `all_combinations` expansion\n", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "feature", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-02T15:37:59Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T16:19:08Z", "started_at": "2026-10-02T16:11:20Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-02T16:19:08Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-609", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-byl", "type": "blocks", "created_at": "2026-10-02T15:37:59Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 1, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-byl", "title": "Batch Sweep: Add All Metrics option for single-metric ranking (single-timeframe gate)", "description": "# Batch Sweep: All Metrics \u2014 Single Objective (single-timeframe gate)\n\n## Description\n\nAdd an `\u2605 All Metrics` option to the **Batch Rank Metric** dropdown (`#batch-metric-select`)\nin the Batch Sweep UI. When selected and exactly **one timeframe** is checked, the sweep\nexpands internally into one sequential sub-run per metric (10 total: all entries in\n`optimizer.TARGET_METRICS` excluding the `\"sharpe\"` alias), producing one leaderboard row\nper `symbol \u00d7 metric` pair. The option is **disabled in the UI** (button locked, warning\nshown) whenever more than one timeframe checkbox is active, and the backend enforces this\nwith HTTP 400.\n\n## Canonical Single-Objective Metric Set\n\nSourced from `src/optimizer.py::TARGET_METRICS` (excluding the `\"sharpe\"` alias):\n\n| Key | Direction |\n|---|---|\n| `sharpe_ratio` | maximize |\n| `drawdown_penalized_sharpe` | maximize |\n| `calmar_ratio` | maximize |\n| `sortino_ratio` | maximize |\n| `drawdown_penalized_sortino` | maximize |\n| `ulcer_index` | **minimize** |\n| `profit_factor` | maximize |\n| `net_profit` | maximize |\n| `total_return_pct` | maximize |\n| `win_rate` | maximize |\n\n## Backend Changes\n\n### `src/app.py` \u2014 `BatchOptimizeRequest`\nNo structural change needed. `target_metric: str = \"sharpe_ratio\"` already accepts\narbitrary strings. The sentinel value `\"all_metrics\"` is intercepted before\n`BatchOptimizerConfig` is constructed.\n\n### `src/app.py` \u2014 `start_batch_optimize`\n```python\nALL_SINGLE_METRICS = [\n    \"sharpe_ratio\", \"drawdown_penalized_sharpe\", \"calmar_ratio\",\n    \"sortino_ratio\", \"drawdown_penalized_sortino\", \"ulcer_index\",\n    \"profit_factor\", \"net_profit\", \"total_return_pct\", \"win_rate\",\n]\n\nif req.target_metric == \"all_metrics\":\n    if len(req.timeframes) != 1:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=400,\n            detail=\"'all_metrics' requires exactly one timeframe to be selected.\"\n        )\n    configs = [\n        BatchOptimizerConfig(\n            ...shared fields from req...,\n            timeframes=req.timeframes,   # single-element list\n            target_metric=metric,\n            enable_multi_objective=False,\n        )\n        for metric in ALL_SINGLE_METRICS\n    ]\n    background_tasks.add_task(_run_all_metrics_batch_task, configs)\n    return {\"status\": \"started\", \"message\": f\"All-metrics sweep started ({len(configs)} metrics).\"}\n```\n\n### `src/app.py` \u2014 `_run_all_metrics_batch_task`\nNew background task function (not modifying `_run_batch_task`):\n```python\ndef _run_all_metrics_batch_task(configs: list[BatchOptimizerConfig]) -> None:\n    from src.batch_optimizer import _update_state\n    for i, cfg in enumerate(configs):\n        if get_batch_state().get(\"cancelled\"):\n            _update_state(running=False, error=\"Batch sweep cancelled\")\n            return\n        # Patch current_combo to include metric context\n        _update_state(current_combo=f\"[{cfg.target_metric} \u2014 {i+1}/{len(configs)}]\")\n        try:\n            BatchOptimizer(cfg).run()\n        except Exception as exc:\n            _update_state(running=False, error=str(exc))\n            return\n    _update_state(running=False, done=_batch_state.get(\"total\", 0))\n```\n\n### Progress Accounting\n`_update_state(total=len(symbols) * len(ALL_SINGLE_METRICS))` \u2014 each `symbol \u00d7 metric`\ncounts as one combo for progress. Timeframe is fixed (single), so it does not multiply.\nThe per-metric `BatchOptimizer.run()` must call `_update_state(done=...)` incrementally.\nReview whether `BatchOptimizer.run()` increments `done` itself or if the wrapper must.\nAdjust as needed to avoid double-counting.\n\n## Frontend Changes\n\n### `src/web/index.html` \u2014 `#batch-metric-select`\nAdd as **first** `<option>`:\n```html\n<option value=\"all_metrics\">\u2605 All Metrics (Single Timeframe Only)</option>\n```\nAdd a hint `<small>` element directly below the `<select>`:\n```html\n<small id=\"batch-all-metrics-hint\" style=\"display:none; color: var(--accent-amber);\">\n  \u26a0 All Metrics mode runs one sweep per metric. Select exactly one timeframe.\n</small>\n```\n\n### `src/web/app.js` \u2014 `syncBatchMetricUI()`\nNew function, called on `#batch-metric-select` change and on every `.batch-tf-check` change:\n```js\nfunction syncBatchMetricUI() {\n  const metricVal = document.getElementById(\"batch-metric-select\")?.value;\n  const tfChecked = [...document.querySelectorAll(\".batch-tf-check:checked\")].length;\n  const hint = document.getElementById(\"batch-all-metrics-hint\");\n  const runBtn = document.getElementById(\"batch-run-btn\");\n\n  if (metricVal === \"all_metrics\") {\n    if (hint) hint.style.display = \"block\";\n    if (tfChecked !== 1) {\n      hint.textContent = \"\u26d4 All Metrics requires exactly ONE timeframe. Please deselect extras.\";\n      hint.style.color = \"var(--accent-red, #ff007a)\";\n      if (runBtn) runBtn.disabled = true;\n    } else {\n      hint.textContent = \"\u2605 All Metrics: will run 10 sweeps (one per ranking metric) for the selected timeframe.\";\n      hint.style.color = \"var(--accent-amber, #ffaa00)\";\n      if (runBtn) runBtn.disabled = false;\n    }\n  } else {\n    if (hint) hint.style.display = \"none\";\n    if (runBtn) runBtn.disabled = false;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWire in the DOMContentLoaded listener block:\n```js\ndocument.getElementById(\"batch-metric-select\")\n  ?.addEventListener(\"change\", syncBatchMetricUI);\ndocument.querySelectorAll(\".batch-tf-check\")\n  .forEach(el => el.addEventListener(\"change\", syncBatchMetricUI));\n```\n\n### `startBatchSweep()` \u2014 client-side guard\nBefore the `fetch` call, add:\n```js\nif (targetMetric === \"all_metrics\" && timeframes.length !== 1) {\n  alert(\"All Metrics mode requires exactly one timeframe. Please deselect extras.\");\n  return;\n}\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `#batch-metric-select` has `\u2605 All Metrics` as first option with value `all_metrics`\n- [ ] Hint element appears when `all_metrics` is selected\n- [ ] Run button is disabled (red hint) when `all_metrics` + multiple timeframes\n- [ ] Run button is enabled (amber hint) when `all_metrics` + exactly one timeframe\n- [ ] `startBatchSweep()` client-side guard prevents dispatch if multiple TFs (defense-in-depth)\n- [ ] Backend receives `target_metric: \"all_metrics\"` and expands to 10 sequential configs\n- [ ] Backend returns HTTP 400 if `all_metrics` + `len(timeframes) != 1`\n- [ ] Each sub-run saves its own leaderboard row with the correct `target_metric` label\n- [ ] Progress bar shows `[metric_name \u2014 N/10]` in the current combo label\n- [ ] All 451 existing tests pass; add \u22651 unit test for the `all_metrics` expansion path\n", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "feature", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-02T15:37:47Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T16:08:26Z", "started_at": "2026-10-02T15:38:52Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-02T16:08:26Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 1, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.14", "title": "Represent short opens with side-correct ledger transactions", "description": "PaperTradingEngine opens both longs and shorts through PaperLedger.record_buy, which records transaction type BUY and positive asset_qty. Short closes are represented as BUY_TO_COVER, but there is no corresponding SELL_SHORT opening event. This makes the supposedly auditable ledger ambiguous and breaks signed-asset/cash-flow reconciliation for short positions, even where the reserved-collateral balance math is intentionally simulated.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Define transaction types and signed cash/asset deltas for long entry/exit and short sale/cover under the paper collateral model\\n- [ ] Route short entry through an explicit short-sale ledger operation, not record_buy\\n- [ ] Make ledger history reconstruct position quantity, reserved collateral, fees, and cash from transactions\\n- [ ] Verify transaction balance_after values and full ledger-to-position reconciliation for profitable and losing shorts\\n- [ ] Preserve or migrate legacy BUY-tagged short entries using position metadata where possible", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:03:58Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T22:51:35Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T21:57:42Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T22:51:35Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.14", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:03:58Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.12", "title": "Reduce repeated paper polling work and lock contention", "description": "evaluate_symbol holds a single engine lock across candle retrieval, indicator generation, and ledger work. step_all_active_profiles fetches/recomputes for every profile, including duplicate symbols/timeframes, so one slow provider call blocks all symbols and repeated profiles multiply work. Poll state and _last_evaluations also grow without an explicit retention policy. Profile workloads and redesign synchronization/caching without weakening per-position idempotency.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Measure poll latency and provider/indicator work by active profile count\\n- [ ] Reuse a candle/indicator snapshot for profiles sharing an exchange/symbol/timeframe on one poll\\n- [ ] Avoid holding a global lock across remote data fetches while retaining per-position serialized settlement\\n- [ ] Bound/expire in-memory evaluation state and prevent overlapping poll cycles\\n- [ ] Add concurrency tests for poll/manual API interaction and benchmark smoke coverage", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "task", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:26Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T23:09:55Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T22:52:53Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T23:09:55Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.12", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:26Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.11", "title": "Bound and validate paper ledger cash operations", "description": "PaperLedger.deposit accepts negative amounts and withdraw accepts negative amounts, allowing cash creation or inverted withdrawals. Related ledger APIs should reject non-finite, zero, or negative cash operations and ensure records cannot drive balance below policy limits. Review whether raw record_sell is permitted to create unbacked inventory outside a valid short workflow.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Require finite positive amounts for deposits and withdrawals\\n- [ ] Define and enforce whether withdrawal may exceed cash or create negative balances\\n- [ ] Restrict sell/short ledger operations to an authorized position workflow or document intentional behavior\\n- [ ] Ensure failed validation writes no transaction and leaves balances unchanged\\n- [ ] Add boundary tests for negative, zero, NaN/infinite, and over-balance operations", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:25Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T22:51:35Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T21:57:41Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T22:51:35Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.11", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:25Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-l7v.10", "title": "Preserve paper price precision and holding-period metrics", "description": "Entry, current, stop, and target prices are rounded to four decimal places in the paper engine, which can collapse micro-cap crypto prices (for example, sub-0.0001 tokens) to zero or materially distort PnL. Normal stop/target exits and reconciliation hardcode holding_period_bars=1 regardless of actual elapsed bars; manual close uses zero. Define asset-aware price precision and consistent holding-period semantics.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Preserve sufficient price precision for micro-priced crypto while respecting stock tick-size policy if modeled\\n- [ ] Keep stored entry/exit/stop/target values internally unrounded or round only at a documented output boundary\\n- [ ] Derive holding_period_bars from processed candle identity across normal, manual, timeout, and reconciliation exits\\n- [ ] Add tests at micro-token price scales and for multi-bar trade duration reporting", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:24Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T22:51:35Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T21:57:42Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T22:51:35Z", "close_reason": "Closed", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-l7v.10", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-l7v", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T04:01:24Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "metadata": "{}"}], "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
