{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-8ig", "title": "Process-based Optuna optimization architecture", "description": "Design and implement an opt-in, measured multi-process Optuna backend for EMA/VWAP optimization. The current optimizer runs a nested objective closure that captures optimizer/config/data state, uses default in-memory study storage, and performs Python-heavy backtests; simply wrapping it in a process pool would not share trials safely or transfer large candle/indicator frames efficiently. Preserve current sequential behavior and avoid promising speedup unless representative benchmarks demonstrate it.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Choose and document supported execution modes and single-host versus multi-node scope\\n- [ ] Establish a picklable worker/objective and bounded data-transfer contract\\n- [ ] Coordinate worker trials through storage supported for the selected process topology\\n- [ ] Integrate process lifecycle, progress, cancellation, errors, and cleanup with API/background and batch flows\\n- [ ] Preserve exact trial budgets and explicit per-worker sampler-seed policy\\n- [ ] Validate correctness, recovery, serialization, and measured throughput before enabling by default", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "epic", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:36:39Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-02T00:45:54Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-02T00:45:54Z", "close_reason": "Epic ema_vwap-8ig completed: all 6 subtasks (8ig.1 - 8ig.6) implemented and verified. Delivered Windows-safe multi-process Optuna backend, picklable worker contracts, journal file locking, API lifecycle/bounded cancellation integration, batch sweep integration, and benchmark certification.", "dependency_count": 0, "dependent_count": 0, "comment_count": 0}
{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.7", "title": "Investigate faster Optuna parallel execution backend", "description": "Warmed benchmarks show Optuna n_jobs=2 is slower than n_jobs=1 on the current Python-heavy workload: 300-bar/10-trial runs were about 0.099-0.104s versus 0.089s, and 1,000-bar runs were about 0.103-0.126s versus 0.088s. Evaluate process-based or other parallel execution, or explicitly constrain/document supported concurrency if no safe speedup is available.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Benchmark warmed 1-, 2-, and higher-worker runs across small and representative datasets\\n- [ ] Evaluate process-based execution with safe data transfer and independent Optuna state\\n- [ ] Keep or change n_jobs behavior based on measured throughput, not assumptions\\n- [ ] Document deterministic guarantees and supported parallel modes\\n- [ ] Add regression/performance smoke tests for the chosen behavior", "notes": "Optuna n_jobs is thread concurrency, not multiprocessing; UI/config/result metadata now say optuna_threads versus sequential. Warmed 300-bar/10-trial sequence measured n_jobs=1 at 0.062s versus 2 and 4 at 0.072s; warmed 1,000-bar runs measured 1 at 0.088s versus 2 at 0.103-0.126s. Cold first runs were excluded due import/startup bias. No process backend was added: current objective closes over the optimizer, dataframe, and shared indicator frame; safe multiprocessing would need independent/shared persistent study storage, deterministic sampler coordination, and controlled dataframe transfer, outside a low-risk fix. Keep default n_jobs=1, allow threaded concurrency as an opt-in without claiming acceleration; reproducible=false for n_jobs != 1. Validation: full suite 384 passed, 2 skipped; diagnostics and diff check clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "task", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T03:05:49Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_a