{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.6", "title": "Reduce repeated work and make Optuna runs reproducible", "description": "Every trial constructs a BacktestEngine and recomputes candidate-independent features over the full dataset. Optuna n_jobs uses concurrent threads while the simulation loop is Python-heavy, so parallel settings may add contention rather than throughput. The sampler seed is hard-coded to 42 and global warning filters are modified at import time. Measure the hot path and improve shared-feature reuse, execution strategy, configurable reproducibility, and warning isolation based on profiling.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Profile a representative study and establish trial-time/throughput baselines\\n- [ ] Reuse safe candidate-independent indicator/data calculations across trials\\n- [ ] Verify n_jobs behavior improves or does not regress throughput for supported workloads\\n- [ ] Make sampler seed explicit/configurable and record it in results\\n- [ ] Avoid process-wide warning suppression from importing the optimizer", "notes": "Implemented sampler_seed (default 42, None for unseeded) through OptunaConfig, optimize API, and batch config; responses report sampler_seed and reproducible only for seeded single-job, no-timeout studies. Removed process-wide warnings.filterwarnings and scoped ExperimentalWarning suppression to sampler creation. Profiled 3,000-bar runs: indicator computation 0.0111s of 0.02617s full backtest; shared VWAP/slope/ATR/volume features are now computed once per study, with EMA columns recomputed per candidate. Warmed cached 3,000-bar backtest median was 0.01542s versus 0.02532s full (39.1% faster); parity tests cover crossover, multi-EMA, and pullback. Warmed n_jobs=2 was slower than n_jobs=1 on 300- and 1,000-bar samples, so the default remains 1; process-backend follow-up is ema_vwap-pbo.7. Validation: full suite 383 passed, 2 skipped; diagnostics and diff check clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "t