{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.5", "title": "Label in-sample optimization results and route robustness checks", "description": "Optuna selects and reports parameters using the same candle set used to score every trial. WFO exists separately, but direct optimization results can be applied or deployed without an out-of-sample check, encouraging winner's-curse overfitting. Clearly label optimization metrics as in-sample and make the supported robustness workflow explicit or enforceable before deployment.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Mark Optuna scores and best_backtest_result as in-sample in API/UI contracts\\n- [ ] Define how WFO/OOS validation is linked to an optimization result before deployment\\n- [ ] Prevent in-sample metrics from being presented as validation evidence\\n- [ ] Add integration tests for the optimization-to-validation workflow", "notes": "Optimizer responses, top trials, Pareto entries, and best_backtest_result now carry evaluation_scope=in_sample. The UI labels scores IN-SAMPLE ONLY, clears stale validation on each new optimization, binds validation to the exact current params snapshot, and keeps deployment disabled until that candidate validates. Optuna-origin paper deployment includes the validation report and is rejected server-side without a report; manual profile deploys remain compatible. Validation: optimizer/API/UI/parameter-flow/validator tests 68 passed; diagnostics, JS syntax, and diff checks clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "task", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:07Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:59:08Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T02:39:31Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T02:59:08Z", "close_reason": "Labeled all optimization metrics as in-sample and connected matching robustness validation to Optuna deployment.", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-pbo.5", "depends_on_id": "ema_vw