{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-pbo.4", "title": "Honor batch min-trades and validate relational search bounds", "description": "BatchOptimizerConfig.min_trades is currently replaced by an adaptive count, so caller configuration is ignored despite being logged. Search validation checks each interval independently but not cross-parameter feasibility such as fast < slow < trend; static delta ranges can therefore generate many pruned candidates or an unusable study. Define precedence between configured and adaptive trade floors and reject or construct relationally feasible EMA bounds before running Optuna.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Honor an explicitly configured min_trades value or document a deliberate adaptive override\\n- [ ] Validate cross-EMA constraints and derived delta intervals\\n- [ ] Avoid spending trials on impossible EMA combinations\\n- [ ] Add batch tests proving min_trades affects both objective and persistence eligibility", "notes": "BatchOptimizer now passes cfg.min_trades into Optuna and uses the same configured threshold for persistence; tests prove the value is not replaced by the candle-count heuristic. Multi-EMA and auto-mode searches derive static fast/slow-delta/trend-delta bounds whose full rectangle satisfies configured EMA bounds and strict fast < slow < trend; infeasible relational configurations fail before study creation. Seeded baselines use the same feasible intervals. Validation: pytest tests/test_optimizer.py tests/test_portfolio_rebalancer.py tests/test_wfo.py -q (49 passed, 1 skipped); diagnostics and diff check clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T02:24:06Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:38:09Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T02:34:22Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T02:38:09Z", "close_reason": "Honored configured batch trade floors and eliminated infeasible 