{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-4ix.3", "title": "Guard Calmar annualization for short backtests", "description": "Short-duration positive backtests can overflow the geometric Calmar annualization exponent. A five-minute profitable stock fixture produced a RuntimeWarning and non-finite annualized return. Define a statistically defensible short-horizon policy and ensure resulting metrics remain finite and serializable without distorting longer-window behavior.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Reproduce overflow with a deterministic short-horizon profitable backtest\\n- [ ] Choose and document a minimum-horizon or stable numerical policy for annualized Calmar\\n- [ ] Ensure Calmar remains finite for short positive and negative samples\\n- [ ] Add regression coverage for API/optimizer-safe metric values", "notes": "Calmar policy: report 0.0 (undefined) when the observed history is shorter than 90 calendar days; for longer histories retain annualized geometric return divided by fractional maximum drawdown. This avoids explosive/noisy annualization on intraday samples while preserving the conventional calculation on quarter-or-longer samples. Regression covers positive and negative five-minute returns plus strict JSON serialization and the longer-window CAGR formula. Validation: full suite 365 passed, 2 skipped; diagnostics and diff check clean.", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "assignee": "Hermes Agent", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T01:56:39Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:12:42Z", "started_at": "2026-10-01T02:09:19Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T02:12:42Z", "close_reason": "Added a 90-day minimum history policy for Calmar and verified finite serialization on short positive/negative samples.", "dependencies": [{"issue_id": "ema_vwap-4ix.3", "depends_on_id": "ema_vwap-4ix", "type": "parent-child", "created_at": "2026-10-01T01:56:39Z", "created_by": "Hermes A