{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-4ix.2", "title": "Backtest execution audit: cost model, slippage, leverage, and edge-case behavior", "description": "Review the execution model for market entries and exits, slippage handling, stock regulatory fees, margin checks, leverage caps, and end-of-data liquidation behavior. Ensure the model reflects the intended asset class, and that fees and costs are applied consistently across the entire lifecycle of each trade.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Confirm entry and exit fees include all relevant costs for crypto and stock trades\\n- [ ] Check slippage and fill-price logic relative to signal timing and overnight gaps\\n- [ ] Verify leverage caps and margin conditions are enforced consistently\\n- [ ] Validate end-of-data close behavior matches the same realized-cost convention as normal exits\\n- [ ] Add targeted tests for stock and low-equity edge cases", "notes": "Implementation in progress: trade.pnl and pnl_pct now include entry and exit fees while portfolio equity applies entry fees once; stock regulatory fees now apply to sell transactions (long exits and short entries); actual risk-sized stock notional is checked against configured buying power under the global 3x cap. Added normal-exit, end-of-data, short-sale-fee, and oversized-short regressions. Combined validation: pytest tests/test_backtester.py tests/test_stock_execution.py tests/test_new_metrics.py tests/test_optimizer.py -q (33 passed); diagnostics and diff check clean. Remaining: decide/test active-position liquidation when equity breaches min_margin_equity; same-close signal timing is separately tracked in ema_vwap-4ix.4. Short-horizon Calmar overflow tracked in ema_vwap-4ix.3.\nExecution audit acceptance completed for fees, costs, end-of-data consistency, and margin edge cases. Trade PnL and pnl_pct include full lifecycle fees while account equity debits entry fees once; stock SEC/FINRA fees are charged on sell transactions; risk-sized notional obeys buying