{"_type": "issue", "id": "ema_vwap-4ix", "title": "Backtest system audit and hardening", "description": "Review the backtest engine for mathematical correctness, execution realism, and performance-metric integrity. Validate equities, fees, slippage, event logic, risk controls, and annualization assumptions against the strategy contract. Produce concrete fixes for any bug, edge case, or efficiency issue discovered.", "acceptance_criteria": "- [ ] Review backtest logic against strategy contract and actual order execution semantics\\n- [ ] Check drawdown, Sharpe/Sortino/Calmar, equity curve, and mark-to-market math for correctness\\n- [ ] Review fee, slippage, margin, and exit-cost handling across crypto and stock flows\\n- [ ] Identify efficiency gaps and guardrails for unstable/degenerate inputs\\n- [ ] Create actionable implementation tasks for fixes and follow-up validation", "notes": "Backtest audit and implementation completed. Corrected baseline-aware drawdown/Sharpe/Sortino/Ulcer calculations, asset-aware annualization, annualized Calmar with a 90-day minimum history, lifecycle fee accounting, sell-side stock regulatory charges, actual-notional buying-power enforcement, stock margin-call liquidation, and next-open execution of close-derived signals. Regression coverage spans final-bar signals, signal-bar indicators, intrabar stop/target precedence, gaps, reversals, crypto/stock fees, margin, and metric serialization. Validation: full pytest suite 365 passed, 2 skipped; diagnostics and diff checks clean. Model caveat: stock margin-call detection is evaluated at bar close, so intrabar equity breaches that recover before close are not modeled.", "status": "closed", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "epic", "owner": "hermes-agent-nous-research@users.noreply.github.com", "created_at": "2026-10-01T01:45:17Z", "created_by": "Hermes Agent", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T02:13:04Z", "closed_at": "2026-10-01T02:13:04Z", "close_reason": "All four audit and implementation children 